    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `membershipTier` value is computed at response-mapping time in `OwnerMapper`, so I added the GOLD rule there \u2014 it takes precedence over the existing SILVER/BRONZE logic.\n\n**`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `membershipTier(Owner)` now first checks whether the owner belongs to a household: if it has a non-blank `householdId` shared by **3 or more** owners (counted via `ownerRepository.findAll()`), it returns `\"GOLD\"`. Otherwise it falls through to the unchanged SILVER (no namesakes + email present) / BRONZE rules.\n\nThis fits the existing pipeline naturally: `AssignHousehold` already assigns/back-fills a shared `householdId` across household members during the `POST /api/owners` flow, so by the time the created owner is fetched back all members carry the same id and the count reflects the household size after the create.\n\nTest results:\n- `AcceptanceTest.coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold` \u2014 passes (third member reports `GOLD`).\n- Full suite \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests pass.",
